feat 1.0

# ADR-0034: the negation of a list that holds a matcher does not say which item differs; refused as MALFORMED_SYNTAX with a hint to negate a field inside an item. (`not` over a literal list stays a literal operand.)

spec SPEC-BAD-131 "Negated list that holds a matcher"
context Bad
aggregate Thing
type command
status draft

construct:
  handler at src/do-thing.ts
  touches src/**

enforce:
  do the thing

contract:
  input ThingInput
  response ThingResult
  record ThingRow

scenario "does the thing":
  when: DoThing { value: 1 }
  predict success:
    response OK ThingResult
    eventStore has [ Wrote with ThingRow { members: not [ { name: "a", text: any string } ] } ]
